-- =====================================================================
-- Bookworm Delta - Bulk-imported catalogue + covers
-- =====================================================================
-- Optional. Run this AFTER 02_seed.sql (same bookworm_app login) to add
-- the rest of the real catalogue - the 59 titles from
-- "Books DATA/Prod Master Table.xlsx" - plus the cover images that
-- ExcelProductImportService could actually match against
-- "Books DATA/Book Covers/" (see ExcelProductImportService.
-- findCoverByTitle). Matching covers by filename against a title only
-- works when the two are actually close - some filenames in that folder
-- have a spelling difference from the spreadsheet's title (a real typo
-- in the source data, not a bug), so 20 of the 59 titles below have a
-- cover and the rest don't - upload the rest by hand from
-- Admin > Products if needed, same as any book with no cover.
--
-- This file is a straight data dump of what that bulk-upload run
-- produces against a freshly-seeded database (02_seed.sql run first, so
-- product_id starts at 9, author_id at 6, etc.) - it exists so that
-- cloning this project and running the three files in database/ gets
-- the same cover-illustrated catalogue on every machine, without
-- needing to repeat the bulk-upload from Admin by hand.
-- =====================================================================

USE bookworm_delta;

-- Titles and descriptions below are Devanagari (Marathi/Hindi). Windows'
-- mysql client otherwise negotiates the terminal's codepage (cp850) as
-- the connection charset instead of the utf8mb4 this data actually is,
-- which garbles those columns and can overflow product_description_short
-- (VARCHAR(255)) on import - see 01_schema.sql's CHARACTER SET utf8mb4.
SET NAMES utf8mb4;


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- New reference rows the import created (author / publisher / genere /
-- product_type_master) - anything already matching a 02_seed.sql row
-- (e.g. the four languages, 'eBook', 'Audiobook') was reused instead.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------

